## Framework-managed folders — don't hand-edit

⚠️ **`how-to/llm-wiki/` and `wiki/project/best-practices/framework/` are shipped by the framework** and are replaced when the framework refreshes a project's docs (`new-wiki.py --phase docs`). If you edit these files in place, your changes get lost on the next refresh.

**Want to customize?** Put your additions in a separate location:

| Where it lives | What goes there | Survives refreshes? |
|---|---|---|
| `how-to/llm-wiki/` | Framework-shipped usage docs | ❌ Replaced on refresh |
| `wiki/project/best-practices/framework/` | The framework's own contract docs (frontmatter, authoring, cycle format) | ❌ Replaced on refresh |
| `wiki/project/best-practices/` | **Your project's** conventions and best practices | ✅ Yours forever |
| `how-to/<your-folder>/` | **Your project's** how-to docs | ✅ Yours forever |
| Anywhere else under `wiki/` | Project-specific entries | ✅ Yours forever |

Paths are relative to this README (the wiki root).

(V2 will support proper user-override layering — for v1, keep your own pages outside the framework-managed folders.)

## How-to folder

`how-to/` holds one folder per installed package; the framework's own is `how-to/llm-wiki/` (entry page `llm-wiki.md`, the user guide `user-guide.md`, one page per skill under `skills/`). Start with `how-to/llm-wiki/user-guide.md`. **Framework-managed** — see the warning above.

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or the `_INDEX.md` files — they're auto-generated by `wiki-map-compile.py`, `wiki-index.py` and `wiki-index-per-folder.py`
- Don't suppress contradictions in `wiki/` — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked, never delete the minority view
- Don't move staged entries into `wiki/` by hand — they wait in `_inbox/proposed/` (beside `wiki/`) and `/wiki-promote` moves them

